# punused findings adjudicated as false positives. One literal substring per
# line, matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason. Invalid-by-construction classes: `.kiro/steering/tools.md`.
#
# Every entry below is an interface method the runtime dispatches through, or a
# constructor other packages' tests own. punused resolves explicit call sites
# only, so a method reached by interface satisfaction reads as unreferenced no
# matter how load-bearing it is. Cross-checked with `deadcode -test ./...`,
# which reports none of them. Upstream: bep/punused#3.
#
# encoding/json contract. Each of these is the UnmarshalJSON the decoder calls
# through the json.Unmarshaler interface while parsing a Fribb mapping record,
# and each exists because the upstream feed types a field loosely: offsetPair
# and flexString/flexInt absorb number-or-string, tmdbID absorbs a scalar or an
# array, stringList absorbs a string or a list. Deleting any one does not remove
# a call site, it silently changes how that field decodes -- a real-data parse
# failure, not a cleanup. Their tests are the only EXPLICIT callers because the
# production path goes through json.Unmarshal.
method (*offsetPair).UnmarshalJSON
method (*flexString).UnmarshalJSON
method (*tmdbID).UnmarshalJSON
method (*flexInt).UnmarshalJSON
method (*stringList).UnmarshalJSON
#
# error + httpx retry contracts. rateLimitedError.Error satisfies `error`, so it
# is what every log line and wrap of an AniList 429 prints; IsTransient and
# RetryAfterHint are the two optional interfaces httpx probes on a returned
# error to decide whether to retry and how long to wait. All three are reached
# by interface assertion inside the library, never by a call this module writes,
# so removing them would not break a build -- it would silently turn a
# rate-limited AniList response into a permanent failure with no backoff.
method (*rateLimitedError).Error
method (*rateLimitedError).IsTransient
method (*rateLimitedError).RetryAfterHint
#
# StaleMapError.Error satisfies `error` and Unwrap upholds the
# errors.Is/errors.As traversal the type documents; both are runtime dispatch
# gopls cannot resolve to a reference.
method (*StaleMapError).Error
method (*StaleMapError).Unwrap
#
# NewIndex (mapping.go:161) is the package's exported constructor over the
# unexported buildIndex production uses (mapping.go:186, via Loader.Load). Its
# callers are four other packages' test suites (mapping, audit, match), which is
# what it is for: an Index built from a literal record slice, with no loader, no
# cache and no network. Deleting it would leave those packages unable to
# construct the type they consume.
function NewIndex
#
# Torrent.Tags is a decode target on the SeaDex DTO, populated by encoding/json
# from the API's `tags` array. EU1002 (no reference at all) is accurate on this
# branch and the field is still not dead: it carries the release's curation tags
# from the wire, and the consumer that reads them is the audit path's curation
# warnings, which lands with the in-flight review branch (where the same field
# is read at internal/audit and bounded during decode). Dropping it here would
# discard data already on the wire and have to be re-added.
field Tags
